    "narrative": "The core of our lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.95), both of whom present as elite daily plays. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a soft matchup against Nick Martinez, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** thrives in his platoon advantage against Carlos Rod\u00f3n, despite a 34% rain risk in his contest. Our highest-leverage play is **Jackson Merrill** (75.27); he is a priority start because of his dynamic platoon advantage against Bailey Ober and his specific utility in the stolen base category, as the matchup projects a high likelihood for him to capitalize on the opposing pitcher's slow delivery.\n\nStrategic platoon edges are fueling several of our mid-tier starts today. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (69.46) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (61.82) both see double-digit boosts to their scores due to favorable platoon splits. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is positioned well to drive runs in the #4 hole against Jos\u00e9 Soriano, and **Luis Robert Jr.** gains significant value hitting against the southpaw Sean Newcomb. Our toughest decision for the final utility spot fell to **Miguel Vargas** (45.53), who ultimately secured the nod over **Dominic Smith** (38.84). While **Miguel Vargas** faced a tougher matchup against Nolan McLean, his xwOBA profile gave him the edge over **Dominic Smith**, whose projected production was stifled by a negative platoon split against Shane Drohan.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the volatile weather in games involving **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Heliot Ramos**, where the 34% rain risk could compress their actual plate appearances. Furthermore, because we are operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status, the current scores for **Liam Hicks**, **Drake Baldwin**, and others are based on projected batting order; should any of these players drop lower in their respective lineups, we may see their efficiency scores dip below our 40-point start threshold. We are holding **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** on the IL, but with the roster depth provided by players like **Nasim Nunez** and **Coby Mayo**, we remain well-positioned to chase the stolen base and RBI volume necessary to climb the standings today.",
